.TH ALTAY 1 "2026-06-07" "altay 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
altay \- modern, touch-friendly, sandboxed file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B altay
.RI [ PATH " | " URI ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Altay
is a Wayland-first, touch-friendly file manager that runs entirely as a normal
user and never requires root. Access is sandboxed to the user's home directory,
mounted removable and external devices, and accessible network shares; system
directories are not exposed.
.PP
It supports archives (zip, tar.*, 7z, rar, deb, rpm and split multi-volume
sets), udisks2 device mounting, gvfs network shares (SMB/SFTP/FTP/WebDAV/NFS)
with passwords stored in the system keyring, image/PDF/video/text previews,
a background transfer queue, an indexed and content search, drag-and-drop,
dark and light themes, and a trash with restore.
.PP
If a path or a network URI (for example
.IR smb://server/share )
is given, Altay opens it on start.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Delete
Move the selection to Trash.
.TP
.B Backspace
Go to the parent folder.
.TP
.B F2
Rename the selected item.
.TP
.B F5
Reload the current folder.
.TP
.B Escape
Cancel path editing / close menu / clear the selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C / Ctrl+X / Ctrl+V
Copy / Cut / Paste.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Select all.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Edit the path / enter a URI.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Focus the search field.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/altay/config.toml
Preferences (hidden files, theme, default view, grid zoom) and saved network
connections.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/altay/
Search index cache and generated thumbnails.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY ", " DISPLAY
Selects the Wayland (preferred) or X11 display.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME
Override the configuration and cache locations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg\-open (1),
.BR udisksctl (1),
.BR gio (1)
